{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787270007689927001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"afeard-technical-kodiakbear","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"d1404dcafa2c2d2f4f6beb32a801754360c40b9aed050f49112607279f3c04f0","event_uuid":"b4248a7f-f35c-45fc-a73b-cc83be90184e","position":{"commit_sha":"cfa9ca4f3ddcb5dcaf0bb397ed6333a2e5077cdc","position":"1787268099312443001-b4248a7f-f35c-45fc-a73b-cc83be90184e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"5b0171172cb36271edf881984131aba987fe5090c7f1e582ee02a213392c5066","event_uuid":"b7a0b6c1-b9b6-4fe0-a812-454342aa457f","position":{"commit_sha":"024a0d0a239d9f3e7d66aa7aa73204abc1efc344","position":"1787268151481173001-b7a0b6c1-b9b6-4fe0-a812-454342aa457f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787268099312443001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b7a0b6c1-b9b6-4fe0-a812-454342aa457f","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"3198-438c-72a5-470f"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nrebar has three detached-child spawn sites that are near-duplicates of one another:\n\n- `src/rebar/_store/push.py` — the async branch of `push_tickets_branch`\n- `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py` — `_spawn_detached_drain` (+ `_detach_kwargs`)\n- `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py` — `_spawn_detached_sweep` (+ `_detach_kwargs`)\n\nEach independently repeats: the `parents[2]` PYTHONPATH bootstrap so a bare-python child can\nimport rebar, the `-c` stub that re-inserts `src` and calls back into rebar, the platform\ndetach flags, the stdio discipline, and the never-raise wrapper. The duplication is not\naccidental and it is documented in the code itself — `compact_trigger._detach_kwargs` says\n\"mirroring :func:`rebar.llm.enrich_drain._detach_kwargs`\", `_spawn_detached_sweep` says\n\"Mirrors ``enrich_drain._spawn_detached_drain``\", and `enrich_drain._spawn_detached_drain`\nsays \"Mirrors push.py's PYTHONPATH bootstrap\".\n\n## Why this matters — a defect has already propagated along this seam\n\nBug `3198-438c-72a5-470f` was a missing `cwd=` on the detached `Popen`: the child inherited\nthe spawning command's working directory, and when that was a `make worktree` worktree since\nremoved, the child died at `os.getcwd()`. It was present at ALL THREE sites, and it got there\nby deliberate imitation across three separate tickets:\n\n- `57114212cf` (2026-06-12, pre-trailer) introduced the pattern in `push.py`;\n- `c1de-d6a0-6cef-4135` copied it into the drain — its plan says outright \"POSIX reuses\n  push.py's approach (`start_new_session=True`, `close_fds=True`) + its PYTHONPATH bootstrap\";\n- `1fde-becd-942a-4351` copied it again into the compaction sweep.\n\nOne omission, replicated three times over two months, because \"spawn a detached rebar child\"\nhas no single implementation to get right once. The next property this pattern needs — a\nsignal handler, an env projection, a resource limit, an fd discipline — will propagate the\nsame way.\n\n## Scope (to be confirmed by whoever claims this)\n- A single `spawn_detached(...)` in `src/rebar/_proc.py` (already the documented single source\n  of truth for logic shared between detached spawn sites, and already home to\n  `reap_process_group` and `detached_child_cwd`; it is a deliberate stdlib-only leaf with no\n  `rebar.*` imports, which must be preserved). It would own the PYTHONPATH bootstrap, the\n  detach flags, the durable cwd, and the never-raise posture; callers would supply only the\n  child entry point and their stderr sink.\n- The three call sites above collapse onto it.\n- Related open question, deliberately NOT changed while fixing 3198: should\n  `_config_sources.repo_root`'s final `Path.cwd()` fallback DEGRADE rather than raise? It was\n  left raising on purpose — a silently-wrong repo root is worse than a loud failure, and the\n  three detached children no longer reach it now that they get an explicit cwd. But the\n  exposure survives for long-lived IN-PROCESS work, which cannot be given its own cwd: daemon\n  threads at `src/rebar/_mcp_writes.py:575`, `src/rebar/llm/workflow/editor.py:523`,\n  `src/rebar/_snapshot/janitor.py:440`,\n  `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/_heartbeat.py:69`, and a reconciler that\n  `src/rebar/config.py:516` says \"can run as a daemon from anywhere\". Decide that posture\n  once, here, rather than per-site.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Exactly one implementation of \"spawn a detached rebar child\" exists; the three sites\n      call it and none re-implements the bootstrap or the detach flags.\n- [ ] A test pins that every detached spawn goes through it, so a fourth site cannot\n      reintroduce the class by copy-paste.\n- [ ] `_proc.py` remains a stdlib-only leaf with no `rebar.*` imports.\n- [ ] A recorded decision (accept or change) on `repo_root`'s cwd fallback for long-lived\n      in-process callers.\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and CI's pytest invocation are green.\n\n## Provenance\nObserved while fixing `3198-438c-72a5-470f`. The cwd omission itself is fixed at all three\nsites; this is the structural reason it was three sites and not one.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"2dc4-9bcd-75b9-4544","ticket_type":"task","title":"consolidate the three detached-spawn sites behind one helper","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b4248a7f-f35c-45fc-a73b-cc83be90184e","b7a0b6c1-b9b6-4fe0-a812-454342aa457f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787270007689927001,"uuid":"062c57d6-2369-4ced-9334-247878a7df4a"}